Subject: [PATCH v2 0/2] Input: add STMicroelectronics FTS5CU56A touchscreen
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

This series adds a driver and a device-tree binding for the
STMicroelectronics FTS5CU56A capacitive multi-touch controller found on
the Samsung Galaxy A52 (a52q) and related devices.

Why a separate driver and not an extension of the existing stmfts.c
(including David Heidelberg's in-flight "Input: support for STM FTS5"
series, patchwork series 1174082):

  Despite the shared "FTS5" generation, the A52's FTS5CU56A runs
  STMicroelectronics' sec_ts-family firmware, whose I2C wire protocol is
  incompatible with the ST reference firmware that stmfts.c (and the FTS5
  extension) target. The reference firmware uses 8-byte events read via
  opcodes 0x85/0x86 and the 0x90-0xa4 command set; the FTS5CU56A uses a
  16-byte event FIFO read via 0x60/0x61 (with the remaining-event count in
  byte 7), ID and firmware-version reads via 0x22/0x24, force calibration
  0x13, a 6-byte 0xfa reset sequence and a different, bit-packed coordinate
  and touch-type event layout. The only byte sequence the two have in
  common is the generic scan enable/disable (0xa0 0x00 0x01/0x00), which
  even collides in meaning (0xa0 is SYSTEM_RESET in the reference set).
  Hosting FTS5CU56A inside stmfts.c would therefore mean bolting a second,
  fully independent event parser and power/configure path onto shared code
  that Heidelberg's series is actively modifying, with no shared behaviour
  to amortise and no hardware here to verify the other two variants. A
  standalone driver is the lower-risk, cleaner result.

The driver is derived from the Samsung downstream driver that is known to
work on the device; the command sequences and timings are preserved
verbatim. This v2 drops the downstream debugging scaffolding (location
strings, per-finger telemetry, verbose logging) and the separate coding
style cleanup patch, so the driver is submitted clean in a single patch.
The compatible is "st,fts5cu56a" (the vendor prefix already carries "st").

Checked with checkpatch.pl --strict (the only remaining report is the
"does MAINTAINERS need updating?" heuristic on the binding-only patch 1/2,
which is resolved by the MAINTAINERS entry added in patch 2/2),
dt_binding_check (no warnings) and a W=1 arm64 cross build of the new
object (no warnings). Not yet tested on hardware for this revision.

